WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.250 --> 00:00:02.737
Navigators hear hard stories all day, often from

2
00:00:02.737 --> 00:00:03.670
their own community.

3
00:00:04.080 --> 00:00:06.760
That has a name: secondary traumatic stress.

4
00:00:07.110 --> 00:00:09.661
The National Child Traumatic Stress Network describes it

5
00:00:09.661 --> 00:00:12.212
as distress that comes from hearing about someone

6
00:00:12.212 --> 00:00:12.850
else's trauma.

7
00:00:13.560 --> 00:00:14.500
What does it look like?

8
00:00:15.050 --> 00:00:18.526
Exhaustion, trouble sleeping, hopelessness, getting cynical, avoiding the

9
00:00:18.526 --> 00:00:19.830
people you serve.

10
00:00:20.240 --> 00:00:22.907
And the risk goes up with things that

11
00:00:22.907 --> 00:00:25.573
fit this work: heavy caseloads, isolation, a lot

12
00:00:25.573 --> 00:00:27.240
of empathy and feeling unprepared.

13
00:00:27.970 --> 00:00:29.150
And then there's the phone.

14
00:00:29.480 --> 00:00:32.535
Community members calling at night, on weekends, at

15
00:00:32.535 --> 00:00:33.680
the grocery store.

16
00:00:34.250 --> 00:00:34.990
Boundary strain.

17
00:00:35.440 --> 00:00:37.616
Saying no can feel like letting your own

18
00:00:37.616 --> 00:00:38.160
people down.

19
00:00:38.470 --> 00:00:40.830
But a kind boundary protects the relationship.

20
00:00:41.340 --> 00:00:43.140
Something like, I want to help with this.

21
00:00:43.490 --> 00:00:45.552
I'm off now, so let's talk tomorrow at

22
00:00:45.552 --> 00:00:45.810
nine.

23
00:00:46.200 --> 00:00:47.940
If it's an emergency, call this number.

24
00:00:48.570 --> 00:00:50.530
Is this mostly on the navigator, then?

25
00:00:50.800 --> 00:00:51.520
Self-care?

26
00:00:52.290 --> 00:00:53.810
Most of it is on the organization.

27
00:00:54.360 --> 00:00:57.800
The fact sheet names balanced caseloads, flexible scheduling,

28
00:00:57.800 --> 00:00:59.520
ongoing training and supervision.

29
00:01:00.030 --> 00:01:01.863
Nobody can self-care their way out of a

30
00:01:01.863 --> 00:01:02.550
caseload that doubled.

31
00:01:03.200 --> 00:01:06.043
So if I supervise a navigator who's gone

32
00:01:06.043 --> 00:01:07.820
quiet and is missing follow-ups?

33
00:01:08.290 --> 00:01:10.842
Meet privately, say what you've noticed without labeling,

34
00:01:10.842 --> 00:01:13.393
ask how they're carrying it and look at

35
00:01:13.393 --> 00:01:14.350
the caseload together.

36
00:01:14.760 --> 00:01:17.049
And make sure they know about confidential help,

37
00:01:17.049 --> 00:01:18.480
like the Employee Assistance Program.

38
00:01:19.130 --> 00:01:22.330
Notice early, share the load and set boundaries

39
00:01:22.330 --> 00:01:22.730
kindly.

40
00:01:23.040 --> 00:01:24.400
That's how the work lasts.
